    "result_text": "All 264 tests pass, including the acceptance tests that pin the structured-address contract. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I implemented\n\nThe request now accepts a **structured address form** (`addressLine1`, optional `addressLine2`, plus the existing `city`/`postcode`), preferred over the flat `address` when present, with full backward compatibility.\n\n**`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added `addressLine1` and `addressLine2` properties to `OwnerFields` (both normalized/stored/returned) and removed `address` from the `required` list, so an owner may satisfy the address requirement in either form. `firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, `telephone` stay required; `address`'s pattern still applies when supplied.\n\n**`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added persistent `addressLine1` / `addressLine2` columns with getters/setters.\n\n**`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 Added the two `address_line*` columns (tests run on hsqldb, which has `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema entry is required).\n\n**`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Let MapStruct map the new fields through to `OwnerDto` (removed the earlier write-only ignores).\n\n**`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Replaced the flat-only address handling with `applyAddress(...)`:\n- If `addressLine1` is non-blank \u2192 normalize it (and `addressLine2` when present) with the existing rules (trim/collapse/upper-case/expand `ST\u2192STREET`\u2026), store the normalized lines on the owner, and return the composed `address` = normalized `addressLine1` + `\" \"` + normalized `addressLine2` (the space+line2 only when line2 is present).\n- Otherwise \u2192 fall back to the normalized flat `address`, leaving the structured lines unset.\n- Neither form \u2192 empty result \u2192 `400`.\n\nThe composed value is stored as `owner.address` before household-hash, postcode-validation and locality computations run, so everything downstream reads the effective (structured-when-present, flat-otherwise) address.\n\nThe `updateOwner` path was left unchanged \u2014 it's outside the create contract exercised by the spec/tests and stays backward-compatible.\n\n**Result:** `Tests run: 264, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS, including `AcceptanceTest.coreNormalizesAndComposesStructuredAddress` (asserts `addressLine1` \u2192 `\"10 KING STREET\"` and composed `address` \u2192 `\"10 KING STREET\"`) and the flat-address backward-compat test.",
